## Phase 3: Regression Containment

### Files at Risk

| File | Risk Description | Mitigation Strategy |
|------|------------------|---------------------|
| `app/(store)/products/[...slug]/page.tsx` | Layout changes could break SSR/Suspense streaming | Test data loading, verify Suspense boundaries intact |
| `app/components/features/filters/FilterSidebar.tsx` | Style changes could affect functionality | Verify filter interactions still work (checkboxes, sliders) |
| `app/components/features/filters/PriceRangeSlider.tsx` | Token refactor could break slider behavior | Test min/max validation, clear functionality |
| `app/components/features/products/ProductCard.tsx` | Hover changes could impact clickability | Verify Link wrapping, button click handlers |
| `app/components/features/products/ProductGrid.tsx` | Grid changes affect responsive behavior | Test all breakpoints (xs, md, lg) |
| `app/components/skeletons/*.tsx` | Skeleton changes must match final layout exactly | Visual regression test (screenshot comparison) |

### Pre-Sprint Baseline
**Action:** Run `/test` baseline capture before any changes
```bash
npm run build
npx playwright test --grep "product-discovery" --update-snapshots
```

---

## Scope Lock Rules

**NON-NEGOTIABLE CONSTRAINTS:**

1. **NO** changes to `globals.css` — use Tailwind utilities only
2. **NO** changes to homepage components (`Hero`, `Featured`, etc.)
3. **NO** changes to data structures (Sanity schemas, GROQ queries)
4. **NO** changes to filter logic — visual-only changes to filter UI
5. **NO** additions to tailwind.config.ts during sprint — use existing tokens
6. **NO** new dependencies — work with existing stack (Tailwind, Phosphor icons, next-sanity)

**ALLOWED:**
- New component files for skeletons if missing
- Style-only changes to existing components
- Mobile-specific components (drawer, mobile controls)

---

## RWD Strategy Summary

### Breakpoint Reference
```javascript
// From tailwind.config.ts
screens: {
  "xs": "475px",           // Small phones
  "lg-desktop": "(min-width: 1024px and min-height: 851px)",  // Desktop
  "lg-touch": "(min-width: 1024px and max-height: 850px)",    // Tablet
}
```

### Component Breakpoint Behavior

| Component | Mobile (375px) | Tablet (768px) | Desktop (1280px) |
|-----------|----------------|----------------|------------------|
| **ShopHeader** | Stack, smaller overline | Stack | Stack with full spacing |
| **ProductGrid** | 1 col, gap-4 | xs:2 cols | lg:4 cols, gap-6 |
| **Sidebar** | Hidden (drawer) | Hidden (drawer) | Block, sticky |
| **MobileControls** | Block | Block | lg:hidden |
| **MobileDrawer** | Full overlay | Full overlay | Hidden |

---

## Phase 4: Execution Delegation

### Execution Sequence

```
PHASE 1: All Skeletons (SC1, SC2) — Parallel execution possible
  └─> /implement SC1 (ProductGridSkeleton)
  └─> /implement SC2 (FilterSidebarSkeleton)
  └─> /test — Verify skeleton alignment with final grids

PHASE 2: Core Components (SC3, SC4, SC5, SC6) — Sequential recommended
  └─> /implement SC3 (ShopHeader)
      └─> /test — Verify header presence
  └─> /implement SC4 (FilterSidebar)
      └─> /test — Verify filter functionality intact
  └─> /implement SC5 (PriceRangeSlider)
      └─> /test — Verify slider behavior
  └─> /implement SC6 (ProductCard)
      └─> /test — Verify card hover states

PHASE 3: Mobile Experience (SC7, SC8) — Sequential
  └─> /implement SC7 (MobileControlsBar)
  └─> /implement SC8 (MobileFilterDrawer)
  └─> /test — Mobile viewport testing

PHASE 4: Polish (SC9, SC10) — Parallel
  └─> /implement SC9 (ActiveFilters)
  └─> /implement SC10 (Page Layout)
  └─> /test — Full regression test
```

### Verification Commands per Contract

```bash
# After EACH scope contract:
npm run build

# After Pass 3 completion for each component:
npx playwright test --grep "[ComponentName]"

# Final verification:
npx playwright test --grep "product-discovery"
npm run build && echo "BUILD PASSED"
```

